<title>USA: Grancare Inc says court to hear appeal.</title>
<headline>Grancare Inc says court to hear appeal.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA, Ga. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>GranCare Inc said on Tuesday the Delaware Supreme Court agreed to hear its appeal of an August 8 order that barred its proposed merger with Living Centers of America.</p>
<p>GranCare announced the $1.8 billion merger on May 8, but was later blocked when the Delaware Court of Chancery granted an injunction filed by Vitalink Pharmacy Services Inc and Manor Care Inc. The injunction referred to a non- competition agreement between Manor Care and GranCare entered in February. The appeal will be heard on October 15, GranCare said in a statement.</p>
<p>GranCare provides medical and long-term care services.</p>
</text>
